=============================================================================
rommsync-nx @VERSION@
=============================================================================

On-device RomM sync for a modded Nintendo Switch: a background sysmodule
(sys-rommsync) that syncs your saves and runs the download queue, plus an
Ultrahand / Tesla overlay (ovl-rommsync) to drive it.

  https://github.com/armaatus/rommsync-nx


INSTALL
-------

Unzip this archive onto the ROOT of your SD card, keeping the folder
structure. It merges with what is already there and touches nothing else:

  atmosphere/contents/@TITLE_ID@/exefs.nsp   the sysmodule
  switch/.overlays/ovl-rommsync.ovl                the overlay
  config/rommsync/config.ini.example               a starting configuration

Then, in order:

  1. The sysmodule ships DISABLED. There is no flags/boot2.flag in this
     archive, so nothing runs until you enable it -- use ovl-sysmodules,
     which is also how you stop it again.
  2. Copy config/rommsync/config.ini.example to config/rommsync/config.ini
     and set [server] url to your RomM.
  3. Open ovl-rommsync from the Ultrahand overlay menu and pair. You type a
     short code into RomM in a browser; no password is ever typed on the
     console.


UPGRADING
---------

Unzip a newer release over the top. Only the three files above are replaced.
config.ini, token.dat, device.dat, state.db and queue.json are not in this
archive, so your settings, your pairing and your sync state survive.


